@startuml activity-submission-to-release
title End-to-end process: from submission to released mark (Activity Diagram with swimlanes)

|Student|
start
:Log in and open "My assignments";
:Choose assignment and enter work;
|System|
:Check enrolment and determine
effective deadline (incl. extension);
if (Submission already exists?) then (yes)
  if (Now <= effective deadline\nand not yet marked?) then (yes)
    :Replace work, version + 1,
    keep previous version;
  else (no)
    :Reject resubmission,
    keep original;
    |Student|
    :See error message;
    stop
  endif
else (no)
  if (Now <= effective deadline?) then (yes)
    :Store as SUBMITTED;
  else (no)
    :Store as LATE (never rejected);
  endif
endif
:Notify course lecturer(s);
|Lecturer|
if (Student asks for more time\nwith a good reason?) then (yes)
  :Grant individual extension, or extend
  the deadline for the whole class (v1.1)
  (new deadline + reason);
  |System|
  :Reclassify LATE -> SUBMITTED
  if covered by the extension;
  |Lecturer|
else (no)
endif
:Open submission and read work;
:Enter raw mark and written feedback;
|System|
:Compute days late against effective deadline;
:Apply late-penalty strategy
(10% of max per day, 0 after 3 days);
:Save MARKED + audit entry (who, when, old, new, reason);
:Notify Head of Department;
|Head of Department|
:Review marks awaiting moderation;
repeat
  if (Mark appropriate?) then (yes)
    :Approve;
  else (no)
    :Adjust mark and give reason;
  endif
  |System|
  :Save MODERATED + audit entry;
  |Head of Department|
repeat while (More marks for this assignment?) is (yes)
->no;
:Release moderated marks for the assignment;
|System|
:Set RELEASED + audit entry for each;
:Notify each student;
|Student|
:View final mark, late deduction
and written feedback;
stop
@enduml
